4. Core Design Principles

Policy-based configuration

Administrators define policies which are enforced across the platform.

Example:

Printing restriction = enabled

Applies across:
	•	web application
	•	mobile application
	•	downloaded documents

Governance-aware permissions

Permissions are based on governance roles and forum participation rather than generic system roles.

Examples:
	•	director
	•	governance professional
	•	observer
	•	system administrator

Security by default

Sensitive governance platforms require restrictive defaults and explicit enabling of risky behaviours.

Auditability

All configuration changes must be logged.

